Let's see if I follow the reasoning.

A. A group of people have, in the past, often been insulted as monkeys.

B. There is a monkey on the cover of this book.

C. Therefore, the monkey is a reference to that group of people.

D. Further inference: Anyone who does not recognize that all pictures of
monkeys are references to this group must not be aware of A.

Could you fill in the details of the inference a little more?  There
appears to be a premise A': All uses of an image which has been used in
the past to insult a group of people are insults that group of people. I
think a little more rigor in deriving A' would be helpful.

